          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The abstract of the staging study 'Staging of brain pathology related to sporadic Parkinson's disease' states that lesions initially occur in the dorsal motor nucleus of the glossopharyngeal and vagal nerves and the anterior olfactory nucleus, and proposes a staging procedure based on the topographical extent of the lesions. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12498954/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0ba8321d11ec0916162dd643cc3e577f2caec06b7b035cf6e4bb34fade54ffd6",
