          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A PubMed abstract states the hypothesis that Parkinson's disease comprises a brain-first type, with alpha-synuclein pathology arising in the brain and secondarily spreading to the peripheral autonomic nervous system, and a body-first type, with pathology originating in the enteric or peripheral autonomic nervous system and then spreading to the brain. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32830221/",
