    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In the PET case-control study described in that abstract (37 de novo Parkinson's disease patients: 24 RBD-negative and 13 RBD-positive; plus 22 iRBD patients), the authors report that two-thirds of iRBD patients had normal putaminal FDOPA scans, while RBD-positive Parkinson's disease and iRBD patients showed reduced cardiac MIBG heart:mediastinum ratios compared with RBD-negative patients. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32830221/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:060d0f762061b2b988854d5860fd06588ec0ba3ce43b244615d8bc0a36acd873",
