    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The reviews describe alpha-synuclein as a protein concentrated at presynaptic nerve terminals. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8347623/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ff909d659ff9bd5a4e63ba50186749f1459debc3c96d43309e19ad1f4c8e268d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:543bea46d8bd46917cb9e0e5aa8d2b7a9f3f445f3fbea47fd54ec79ed4466da4",
            "ev:7ac81f2bd60e55b6cc349bd66403cee5ca8f512869435bf5549802a95a7cae05"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/aging-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnagi.2022.907293/full"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The aggregation review describes an amphipathic amino-terminal region of alpha-synuclein with an important lipid-binding role. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8347623/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:06567e5ce03e5caeccedb7a8c3538600911324bc0539d0d144006736617fd248",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:639c2fc7a081f04008de149e85611554e15021bc548578feb9662cd786639247"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The reviews describe conformational templating as misfolded alpha-synuclein recruiting endogenous protein into altered conformations. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8347623/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0a29d4aa296db7e05154f01fe9bbda3a4d3b2c28978629889c82829797fc16c8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:55f5b4591f83a667e5c524ffe344e46f41d1edf741eba2bb9dc3dda687bcfe6b",
            "ev:c7ce37aa392f302caccc0c4975a22c1154c3aee82c14a103dc15028c0d821616"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/aging-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnagi.2022.907293/full"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The aggregation review describes alpha-synuclein fibril formation as typically nucleation-dependent, with lag, elongation and maturation phases. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8347623/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:01c987faa9f3875f9a5ae841ed09ffe0b4503139fcd1d7bfdf9e7d838c3d4fa6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:298f240ab76fab45c84d3cce6c8859d80a02343fcafb1db3579e66a3f9ac2ee9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Luk and colleagues report that intrastriatal synthetic alpha-synuclein fibril inoculation in wildtype non-transgenic mice produced Lewy-like pathology in anatomically interconnected regions. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3552321/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a6e6db3e5d372db3ca374a8f4489a98197906795baafb6ba2a300113d64dc36a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e832d4d39f3279288dd933870b76e3d4ba0ca8953ad9c866fca0e8eaa90ab1b0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the inoculated mouse model, Luk and colleagues report progressive dopamine-neuron loss in the substantia nigra pars compacta accompanying Lewy pathology accumulation. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3552321/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:af94595a10572271528f9d1ba07fe92c528c02e043a6daec3951ce53b15b4d1d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e832d4d39f3279288dd933870b76e3d4ba0ca8953ad9c866fca0e8eaa90ab1b0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Brundin and Melki describe anterograde and retrograde transport of alpha-synuclein assemblies monitored in primary neurons grown in microfluidic devices. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.jneurosci.org/content/37/41/9808",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6db3bafa2cc5af8ba9aad7abe6096d76aab7f3fff08d1259e93daca3f53835c4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b442610c5e95947d628aa577bfd7d401f9391828c97aeed299e49203c65c3dfa"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The aggregation review states that whether small alpha-synuclein oligomers are more toxic than mature fibrils remains uncertain. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8347623/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e6b4e07b50411f80741e3c3fd82287b9e5d09c022735dd085d4e7d25991a2011",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0dc1bb7a789650a4344943cb22387a309b146a337ee90a7538d5c407cc897bcd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Brundin and Melki propose neuron-to-neuron transfer as essential for regional Lewy pathology spread; Surmeier and colleagues argue that the spreading hypothesis is difficult to reconcile with human postmortem and connectome evidence. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.jneurosci.org/content/37/41/9808",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f5160f06462d2fa7c5a4a0f4d1e2673abf08aeb6e2cd3fb4f954f21991649df2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:38b19e22eb36a8f141033f1a4f2f7b5871f5645ddf1833d66e7e4e0605bd75ad",
            "ev:c693ad15e502dddff6cfdb532b8bf1d0815a2f34de1ed9cf0be64025ec6d72cc"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.jneurosci.org/content/37/41/9799"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Surmeier and colleagues caution that the postmortem data motivating staging did not directly establish longitudinal evolution of Lewy pathology within individual brains. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.jneurosci.org/content/37/41/9799",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0f8329b46d01f38eb46f28aa3a2751bd799935861bc739b61725d45b80a9f87c",
